      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page (referenced as [[write-journal]]) describes a mechanism for safely handling file writes. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core function**: Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state in an in-memory write journal \u2014 either the previous content if the file existed, or a note that it didn\u0027t exist.\n\n**Rollback capability**: If an agent run fails (due to a turn cap being exceeded, an unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order:\n- Restore previous content for files that existed\n- Delete any newly created files\n\n**Transaction semantics**: This provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the in-memory journal itself serves as the transaction log for the duration of one run.\n\n**Note on the Query agent**: The Query agent (the one you\u0027re currently using) doesn\u0027t actually use the journal\u0027s rollback path since it has no write tool, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
